# Real-user job: a Claude Code user drops a project-scoped .mcp.json into a
# repo (the way `claude mcp add --scope project` or a hand-written
# .mcp.json would) and expects kiln to pick it up the same way. kiln
# currently only reads ~/.claude.json (or --mcp-config), not project
# .mcp.json, so /mcp is expected to show no servers and the on-call
# investigation has no incidents MCP tools to call. This is a known gap the
# lead is closing; NOTE lines below mark what should change once project
# .mcp.json support lands.
@real
@size 140x45
@fixture qa/fixtures/real/mcp-orders-svc
@setup mkdir -p {PROJ}/../bin && go -C {ROOT} build -o {PROJ}/../bin/incidents ./qa/fixtures/incident-mcp && printf '{"mcpServers":{"incidents":{"command":"%s"}}}' "{PROJ}/../bin/incidents" > {PROJ}/.mcp.json
WAITFOR /describe a task/ 30
SHOT ready
WAIT 4
TYPE /mcp
KEY enter
SHOT mcp-dialog
EXPECT /incidents/
KEY esc
SHOT mcp-dialog-closed
TURN orders-svc is paging... use the incidents MCP to figure out what's wrong, then fix it in this repo and add a regression test
SHOT investigated
RUN go vet ./... && go test ./...
RUN grep -RIl "page=3\|per_page=10\|page: *3" --include=*_test.go . | grep -v vendor
